---
/**
 * The moving background: three blurred fields drifting behind everything.
 *
 * The only decoration in this design system, and it earns its place on one
 * page type — a landing page has to hold someone still for a moment, and a flat
 * near-black rectangle does not. It obeys the same rules the rest of the book
 * sets: two hues and no third, nothing above 14% opacity, no fill under the
 * reading column, and no movement at all under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
 *
 * `fixed` and `-z-10`, so it costs one composited layer and never moves with
 * the content — which also means the whole page scrolls through it, and the
 * fields are sized in viewport units for that reason. The blur is on a transformed element, which keeps it on the
 * compositor rather than repainting the page: three drifting 60vw circles
 * repainted every frame would heat a laptop for no reason.
 *
 * The grain on top is a single inline SVG turbulence — no image request, a few
 * hundred bytes — and it is what stops the gradients from banding on an 8-bit
 * panel, which is what they do over near-black without it.
 */
---

<div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-0 -z-10 overflow-hidden">
  <!-- Accent, top left: the warmest point on the page, behind the heading. -->
  <div
    class="absolute -left-[15%] -top-[25%] h-[75vh] w-[75vw] rounded-full blur-[110px] opacity-[0.22] motion-safe:animate-drift-a"
    style="background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--color-accent) 0%, transparent 68%);"
  >
  </div>

  <!-- Violet, right: the machine-side hue, kept opposite the accent so the two
       never mix into a third colour in the middle of the page. -->
  <div
    class="absolute -right-[20%] top-[8%] h-[65vh] w-[65vw] rounded-full blur-[120px] opacity-[0.17] motion-safe:animate-drift-b"
    style="background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--color-violet) 0%, transparent 70%);"
  >
  </div>

  <!-- A second, dimmer accent low down, so the page does not fade to flat black
       the moment the hero scrolls away. -->
  <div
    class="absolute bottom-[-20%] left-[25%] h-[60vh] w-[60vw] rounded-full blur-[130px] opacity-[0.13] motion-safe:animate-drift-c"
    style="background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--color-accent-bright) 0%, transparent 70%);"
  >
  </div>

  <!-- Grain. 3.5% white noise: enough to break the banding, never enough to
       read as texture. The image itself is in `global.css` — see the note
       there for why it cannot live in a `style` attribute. -->
  <div class="grain absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.035]"></div>
</div>
